{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1478261-dream-sequences-in-scion","id":1478261,"title":"Dream Sequences in Scion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-07T22:49:15-07:00","id":1478261,"title":"Dream Sequences in Scion","content":"So for my next session, Im planning for the characters to have a shared dream sequence, where the characters could learn something about some of the events happenings in the town. The town is in the appalachians, and I have thought of it as a sort, well, daycare is not the right word, but its a place that was founded by a group of scions from different pantheons, as a place where other scions could live in peace away from the conflict between the pantheons or the titans. At least 1 percent of the population are scions, probably more, but most dont know it. <br /> <br /> Anyway, as I said, I was planning for a dream sequence session, one that could show that there is something strange and dark in the town. What recommendations would you give me for such a scene? The characters are still in their origin stage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26500-happilyevil321","name":"happilyevil321","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T23:31:10-07:00","id":1478262,"title":"","content":"For now, I only point that there is <b>Astral</b>-like realm canonically in Scion World.<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion\"> See this topic for details</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T08:56:00-07:00","id":1478371,"title":"","content":"Well, you should consider what the dream sequence is for, exactly. If it is meant to give some clues or just give some ambience to the game then just narrate it without requiring rolls. If it is a sort of dreamquest to gather clues then an Occult roll might be necessary and it would use the investigation rules. Sometimes when using dreams I have players explore the dream freely without restrictions but I have them roll some &quot;mental fortitude&quot; roll or similar to see how long they have to explore and gather answers before the dream collapses.<br /> <br /> If it is full on exploration of astral realms \u00e1 la Inception I would probably have the characters roll their own skills, possibly using mental attributes instead of physical ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T16:28:00-07:00","id":1478521,"title":"","content":"That dreamquest thing Intrigues me. And i like your idea. Should it be like, a sort of dream version of the place they are? Kind of like werewolf umbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26500-happilyevil321","name":"happilyevil321","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}